// Myrnohrad, part II, The road (Дорога): 3 December 2025, the short day. The corridor is about a kilometre wide
// (c15 §3), nothing on wheels gets through by day, and their drones own the road (c15 §5). The plan wanted a clear
// day of 3-7 December; ERA5 has none (design/myrnohrad.md, progress): the 3rd is the least grey of the week, dry and
// calm under 95% cloud, 4 °C, the ground bare. Until the robots and their drones are built (phases 3-8), the day is
// a placeholder: the seep at the clear day's rate, the posts, a KAB pair. The schema is
// bav_core::data and bav_sim::data; the map is map.ron.
(
    date: "3 December 2025",
    tally_date: "03 DEC 2025",
    // 08:00 to sunset, 15:40, in the day's 1500 s.
    day_start_min: 480.0,
    compression: 0.307,
    // No snow yet that week (ERA5: snow depth 0 from 1 to 15 December): the late autumn's bare, frozen ground.
    season: Autumn,
    // 3 December is the 337th day of the year; Kyiv on UTC+2.
    sun: (337, 2.0),
    // Under cloud all day, dry, a light easterly (ERA5: 95% cloud, 9 km/h from the east).
    overcast: true,
    wind: (-2.0, 0.0, -1.55),
    // Half the town's roofs gone by now, more ruins smouldering, the cars of three weeks on the road.
    ruined: (0.5, 11),
    smouldering: 16,
    cars: [
        ((-1445.8, -213.4), 1.28),
        ((-2102.3, -382.4), 1.61),
        ((-517.5, -89.7), 2.04),
        ((721.8, -313.2), -1.4),
        ((-1577.9, -236.6), -1.4),
        ((428.1, -297.3), -1.31),
        ((-614.5, -94.7), -1.76),
        ((332.8, -285.0), -1.69),
        ((-1217.2, -152.5), -1.6),
        ((-1674.8, -263.9), 1.66),
        ((-750.0, -75.8), -1.46),
        ((-1721.7, -285.3), -1.35),
        ((-815.8, -94.3), 1.72),
        ((-449.5, -98.9), 1.12),
        ((168.1, -270.1), 2.22),
        ((-2084.5, -377.9), -1.38),
    ],
    words: (
        briefing: r#"MYRNOHRAD (МИРНОГРАД), THE ROAD INTO THE POCKET
3 DECEMBER 2025, DAY

Two days ago Moscow announced that Pokrovsk had fallen. A NATO official says Myrnohrad is virtually encircled. The
corridor out to the north is a kilometre wide, and the one road in, through Rivne and Svitle, is watched from the
air every hour of the day. Nothing on wheels gets through it in daylight; what comes in comes by robot, by heavy
bomber drone, or on foot at night. The wounded wait.

You are the same drone team, in the same basement. The garrison still holds Svitle, Rivne, the western quarters
and the mine. Their infantry still comes in by twos and threes, fewer on a day like this, and goes for the drone
crews first.

The day will run whether or not you do anything. What you do matters at the margin.

Mouse: right-drag to look, wheel to zoom.  WASD: fly the drone.  Q/E: turn.  R/F: climb/descend.  I: thermal.
Left click: 155 mm fire mission (4 rounds).  4: an FPV.  C: drop a grenade from the drone.
V: a ground robot for the wounded.  Alt+click: a robot with ammunition.  7: the robot's camera.  8: the Vampire.
1/2 or Tab: drone / the observers on the high-rise.  M: move the drone team when they find you.  P: pause.  [ ]: time.

Press Enter."#,
        op_label: "OBSERVERS, A NINE-STOREY ROOF ON SOBORNA STREET (СПОСТЕРІГАЧІ, ДЕВ'ЯТИПОВЕРХІВКА НА СОБОРНІЙ)",
        op_lost: "The observers on the high-rise are gone. No eyes from the roof.",
        forward_belt: "the ruins",
        mine_lines: ["Mine. He's stopped.", "Another one on a mine.", "Mine on the verge. That one's done."],
        closing: [
            "On 8 December the 7th Corps pulled out of the salient south of Pokrovsk. On the 10th the exits from Myrnohrad were reported to be collapsing.",
            "On 27 December Russia claimed Myrnohrad. ISW saw them in about half of it.",
        ],
        keys: "R: the same day again, on the same road.     Esc: quit.",
        sources: [
            (
                publisher: "Euromaidan Press",
                date: "27 Nov 2025",
                title: "Russia doesn't need to storm Myrnohrad—just wait for a sunny day",
                url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/11/27/road-into-myrnohrad/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "European Pravda",
                date: "2 Dec 2025",
                title: "NATO says Myrnohrad is \"virtually encircled\" and Russians control over 95% of Pokrovsk",
                url: "https://www.eurointegration.com.ua/eng/news/2025/12/2/7226211/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Euromaidan Press",
                date: "10 Dec 2025",
                title: "\"Impossible to stop them, they're everywhere\": Ukraine holds Pokrovsk against 170,000 Russians, but Myrnohrad evacuation routes collapse",
                url: "https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/12/10/impossible-to-stop-them-theyre-everywhere-ukraine-holds-13-sq-km-of-pokrovsk-against-170000-russians-but-myrnohrad-evacuation-routes-collapse-video/",
            ),
            (
                publisher: "Institute for the Study of War",
                date: "28 Dec 2025",
                title: "Russian Offensive Campaign Assessment, December 28, 2025",
                url: "https://understandingwar.org/research/russia-ukraine/russian-offensive-campaign-assessment-december-28-2025/",
            ),
        ],
    ),
    // The debrief's rows (the schema is the game's screen.rs); the tally's and the fire panel's lines are map.ron's.
    debrief: (
        rows: [
            Line("Their men sent in", Sent),
            Line("    dead", AttackerDead),
            Line("    came back", Returned),
            Line("Our casualties", DefenderLosses),
            Areas("{area} at the end"),
            Line("Shells left", Shells),
            If(Drops, [Line("Grenades dropped from the drone", Drops)]),
            If(
                Robots,
                [
                    Line("Ground robots", Robots),
                    Line("    loads delivered", Delivered),
                    Line("Wounded brought out by robot", WoundedCarried),
                    Line("    still waiting", WoundedWaiting),
                ],
            ),
            If(Bomber, [Line("The Vampire's sorties", Sorties)]),
            If(
                Seep,
                [
                    Line("Their burrows in the town", Burrows),
                    Line("    found", BurrowsFound),
                    Line("    emptied", BurrowsEmptied),
                    Line("Their fire on our drone crew told", CrewsHit),
                ],
            ),
        ],
    ),
    op: ((868.0, 495.0), 30.0),

    // The pocket on 3 December: the corridor about 1 km wide north of the box (c15 §3); theirs closer on the
    // south-western fields, the south-eastern edge theirs (c15 §2, 14 Nov), the jaw over the north-eastern corner.
    // The road in stays ours to Rivne.
    pocket: (
        grey: [
            [
                (-5000.0, -400.0),
                (-2400.0, -380.0),
                (-1500.0, -50.0),
                (-300.0, 450.0),
                (700.0, 600.0),
                (1600.0, 750.0),
                (5000.0, 600.0),
                (5000.0, 5000.0),
                (-5000.0, 5000.0),
            ],
            [(500.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -150.0), (1700.0, -350.0), (900.0, -1000.0)],
        ],
        theirs: [
            [
                (-5000.0, -250.0),
                (-2400.0, -200.0),
                (-1600.0, 300.0),
                (-400.0, 800.0),
                (700.0, 950.0),
                (1500.0, 1100.0),
                (5000.0, 1000.0),
                (5000.0, 5000.0),
                (-5000.0, 5000.0),
            ],
            [(1000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -5000.0), (5000.0, -500.0), (1800.0, -700.0), (1200.0, -1300.0)],
        ],
    ),
    // The garrison's posts: Svitle, Rivne, the western quarters, the high-rise, the mine, the western entrance.
    ua_positions: [
        (-560.0, -1250.0),
        (-1750.0, -700.0),
        (-100.0, 250.0),
        (500.0, 400.0),
        (880.0, 525.0),
        (1400.0, -300.0),
        (300.0, -150.0),
    ],

    // ---- The battle's part (bav_sim::data) ----
    // Ground robots and a heavy bomber: four robots, the wounded waiting for them, their FPVs on a clear day's road
    // (until phase 3 builds their crews, a chance per kilometre); the Vampire's two sorties for the dusk.
    robots: (ugvs: 4, casevac: true, found_per_km: 0.3, bomber: (sorties: 2, endurance: 900.0)),
    // The Record: riflemen at the seven posts, a battery's sixteen rounds, eight FPVs, eight grenades for the drone.
    allotment: (
        points: 80,
        supply: (6, 1.0),
        record: [
            (id: "rifles", at: 0),
            (id: "rifles", at: 1),
            (id: "rifles", at: 2),
            (id: "rifles", at: 3),
            (id: "rifles", at: 4),
            (id: "rifles", at: 5),
            (id: "rifles", at: 6),
            (id: "155", count: 1),
            (id: "fpv", count: 8),
            (id: "vog", count: 4),
        ],
    ),
    // The day: about ten get in on a day like this (c15 §5), seeping from four sides at about 1.3 men an hour
    // (bav_sim::seep), a KAB pair, the claim of 1 December on the net.
    script: [
        (2.0, Say("Bird up. Cloud, but it's dry. They can see everything today, and so can we.")),
        (
            30.0,
            Say(
                "All, this is {command}. Moscow says Pokrovsk is theirs. It changes nothing here. Nobody on the road by day.",
            ),
        ),
        (
            150.0,
            Seep(
                route: 0,
                from: 450.0,
                width: 300.0,
                per_hour: 0.45,
                crews: 0.6,
                label: "08:45  Twos and threes at the south-eastern edge",
            ),
        ),
        (150.0, Seep(route: 1, from: 700.0, width: 300.0, per_hour: 0.35, crews: 0.4)),
        (150.0, Seep(route: 2, from: 1550.0, width: 300.0, per_hour: 0.25, crews: 0.15)),
        (150.0, Seep(route: 3, from: 1000.0, width: 300.0, per_hour: 0.25, crews: 0.15)),
        (
            600.0,
            Bombs(
                from: (300.0, 100.0),
                to: (500.0, 250.0),
                n: 2,
                label: "11:05  KABs on the western quarters",
                say: "Su-34s. Glide bombs. Down.",
            ),
        ),
        (1350.0, Say("This is {op}. It's getting dark. The road will be busy tonight.")),
    ],
)
